cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "ICE: A Local-First Conversational Memory System and a Longitudinal Evaluation Protocol"
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Deepesh
    family-names: Sonar
    email: 18deepnar@gmail.com
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0008-1762-4246"
    affiliation: "Thakur College of Engineering and Technology, Mumbai"
repository-code: "https://github.com/Deepnar/ice"
abstract: >-
  ICE is a local-first memory layer that sits between a chat client and any
  OpenAI-compatible model, giving it persistent, structured memory of prior
  conversations entirely on the user's own hardware. It combines a six-leg
  hybrid retrieval orchestrator fused with weighted Reciprocal Rank Fusion, a
  bi-temporal knowledge graph in which superseded facts remain retrievable as
  history, and a multi-head classifier that gates whether long-term retrieval
  fires at all. The accompanying protocol, LSREP (Longitudinal State-Replay
  Evaluation Protocol), replays real long-running conversations turn by turn,
  reconstructs the complete memory state at 50 checkpoints, and scores answers
  against a ground truth that evolves as facts are superseded.
keywords:
  - information retrieval
  - long-term memory
  - large language models
  - retrieval-augmented generation
  - knowledge graphs
  - evaluation methodology
  - local-first
license: Apache-2.0
version: v2-paper-eval
date-released: "2026-08-01"
